+ * THE SLIDING APERTURE [D2-G · REGISTRY §6]. Everything that moves is a `translate`, an
+ * `opacity` (with the `visibility` it gates), a seat's `clip-path`, the one ink scalar or
+ * the flow, on WAAPI, so the compositor runs the geometry and the main thread runs no
+ * script between retargets.
+ *
+ * THE BOXES (GlassDock.vue, dock.css). The root stays at its natural layout; nothing
+ * reserves or scales it. The plate sits in an `.dock-aperture` box that covers every
+ * window an episode paints, inside two nested doors: `overflow: clip`, rounded by the
+ * dock's corner, one per moving edge, each counter-translated so the plate stays still
+ * in the page. The visible window is their intersection, a stadium with an exact corner
+ * at every frame. The edge ring's arcs ride the doors as caps; the drop shadow is two
+ * casters clipped at the window's centre; the press surface is the hit pair, two
+ * transparent doors on the same lanes rounded by `clip-path`. `.dock-layers` is the face
+ * door: through an episode it rides the end edge and clips its end side at the window's
+ * end edge (or the end region's start), and its faces ride the start edge.
+ *
+ * THE EPISODE. Every change is one kind of episode: a posture flip, a content change, a
+ * face swap, a leaving seat, or a retarget of any of these mid-flight. At the flip the
+ * DOM already holds the new layout. The carrier takes the OLD painted geometry (the rest
+ * cache at rest, the running lanes mid-flight), reads the NEW natural geometry, and
+ * releases one lane per moving quantity from old to new on the dock rung, carrying the
+ * old velocity:
+ *   a / b    the window's min and max edges (left/top, right/bottom)
+ *   σ(seat)  a seat whose place in its region changed: per-seat FLIP
