+ * Every element's keyframes are a combination of those lanes, sampled on one grid and
+ * started together, so a door and its counter never disagree.
+ *
+ * THE CLOCK [H3-4]. An episode from rest starts PENDING: its animations take their
+ * start time from the first frame that renders them, which is the frame after any
+ * main-thread block that follows the flip; a start the engine reports from before such
+ * a block is moved to the frame after it, so a stall delays the motion instead of
+ * eating it. A retarget mid-flight starts on the time the window paints: the frame's
+ * clock, re-read from the doors' sampled `translate` (an engine may sample on its live
+ * clock), which keeps position and velocity continuous. A replay of an episode no frame
+ * has started yet, or one on a stale frame clock, starts pending too.
